// Test project: src + tests, no emit.
//
// NOT wired into `typecheck` yet, unlike every other package in this workspace.
// Until DAG-332 this file was passed to tsc by nothing at all — `typecheck` is
// `tsc --noEmit`, which resolves tsconfig.json (src only) — so it accumulated
// errors silently. Baseline when first run, 2026-08-21: 100 here, 5 in
// sluice-enrich, 1 in sluice-mcp. The other four packages are now clean and gate
// on this file; this one does not yet.
//
// ponytail: run it by hand with `pnpm typecheck:tests`. ~99 remain, mostly
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess in test bodies plus config literals that drifted from
// their types. Ratchet it down, then append
// `&& tsc -p tsconfig.test.json --noEmit` to this package's `typecheck` script,
// which is all the other four needed. Do NOT loosen this config to make the
// number go down — the errors are the drift signal, not the problem.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
